WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.910
A crane jib and its support cable, drawn
as two arrows on three-dimensional axes.

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.320
From this viewpoint, they
look perfectly perpendicular.

3
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.610
Swing the camera round,
and suddenly they don't.

4
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.280
Perspective is fooling your eyes.

5
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.150
Could a single number, worked
out from their components,

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.750
settle it for good?

7
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.340
In this mission, you'll write each
vector as a column of three components.

8
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.380
You'll multiply matching components,
then add the three results.

9
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.810
And you'll link that single number
to the angle between the two vectors.

10
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.690
Your mission: find how one number can
tell you if two directions meet at right

11
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:38.430
angles.
